Native runtime: Rust, ONNX Runtime, LanceDB/Lance, Apache Arrow, Hugging Face
tokenizers, zbus, libheif and libjpeg-turbo. System libraries are provided by Omarchy packages;
ONNX Runtime is linked into the executable. Dependency licenses remain their
respective owners' licenses. The bundle uses a local LanceDB 0.37.1 manifest
patch that disables optional Jieba/Lindera tokenizers; its runtime source is
unchanged. See LANCEDB-LICENSE for the upstream Apache-2.0 license.

Dependency licenses (ONNX Runtime: MIT; LanceDB/Lance and Arrow:
Apache-2.0; tokenizers: Apache-2.0; zbus: MIT; libheif: LGPL-3.0;
libjpeg-turbo: IJG/BSD/zlib).

CUDA-capable bundles additionally carry ONNX Runtime's CUDA/shared provider
libraries. NVIDIA driver, CUDA 12 and cuDNN 9 libraries are external runtime
requirements and are not redistributed in this bundle. The stdio MCP server
uses rmcp (MIT) and Tokio (MIT).

Audio/video decoding invokes separately installed ffmpeg and ffprobe tools.
Their licensing depends on the system FFmpeg build; no FFmpeg binary is bundled.

First-run EmbeddingGemma 2 FP16 text, vision and audio assets are downloaded from
onnx-community/embeddinggemma-2-ONNX at the exact revision in model-manifest.json.
The export declares Apache-2.0. Upstream model and export:
https://huggingface.co/google/embeddinggemma-2
https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/embeddinggemma-2-ONNX
Preserve the applicable model license and attribution when distributing assets.

This local development bundle is not a published or signed release. Complete
project and third-party license/redistribution review before public distribution.
